  "rule": "Hand-built replay cases for the event model. Each case reaches an edge that no published recording is known to reach in a small enough form for a fast test: two readings that share a track and a case time, two string events at one time, a waveform sample that lands exactly on a second boundary, a record that straddles a second, a second with no sample, two cases of different length so that one room starts its next case while the other room is still active, and a case whose file holds readings before its start and after its whole-second end (the published recordings end within a second of the clinical end time). Times are whole microseconds from the case start. The cases are never mixed with the published recordings and never counted as candidates.",
